{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1554691-supernaturalists-of-district-a-cryptid-hunter-mystery-cult","id":1554691,"title":"Supernaturalists of [district] - a cryptid hunter Mystery Cult","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2025-10-27T06:56:53-07:00","id":1554691,"title":"Supernaturalists of [district] - a cryptid hunter Mystery Cult","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b><i><u><span style=\"font-size:20px\">Supernaturalists of [district]</span></u></i></b></div> <br /> <br /> This is a mostly generic Mystery Cult of cryptid hunters. It can be plugged in any location with notable amounts of magically mutated fauna. Its members stalk the wilderness (or the urban jungle) for them, capture them (preferably alive) and hand them over to the local Athenaeum for study and display, whose liaisons act as the cult's supernatural backers. It organises itself in imitation of Sleeper 19th century naturalist academic cliques.<br /> <br /> <u><b>* Cryptozoology speciality in Occult</b></u><br /> <u><i>Interns</i></u> learn a splattering of knowledge about the creatures they're supposed to track, capture and study.<br /> <br /> <u><b>** Sleepwalker Merit</b></u><br /> If already Sleepwalker<br /> <u><b>** Banner Bearer 1</b></u><br /> If already Awakened<br /> <u><b>** Imbued Ally 1</b></u><br /> Between encounters with their quarry and their Mystagogue handlers, <u><i>Assistants</i></u> have the veil over their soul partially lifted. The most useful effect of this level of initiation and study for their Mage handlers is no longer aggravating Paradox and causing Dissonance, expanding the Awakened's arsenal of spells usable safely around (and on) their subordinates considerably. The side effect of holding additional spells for Supernaturalists who were Sleepwalking or even Awake before reaching this rang of initiation is just the sweet, Perfected cherry on top.<br /> <br /> <u><b>*** Eye for the Strange Merit</b></u><br /> <u><i>Bachelors</i></u> learn to weed out mundane sightings, allowing them to focus on real supernatural encounters of interest to their club and the Mysterium.<br /> <br /> <u><b>**** Advanced Library 3 (Manticores, God-Machine Cryptids, Hedge Beasts)</b></u><br /> <u><i>Doctors</i></u> gain reliable, minimally supervised access to shelves of their patron Caucus' Athenaeum containing information on the most common supernatural animals of the World.<br /> <br /> <u><b>***** Allies (Mysterium) 3</b></u><br /> If already Mystagogue<br /> <u><b>***** Sanctum 3</b></u><br /> <u><i>Professors</i></u> have ingratiated themselves to the local Mysterium to such a degree over their career, that they may petition the Order for mundane and magical assistance relevant to the quarry currently pursued - f.e. to equip members ranked Assistant or above with Mind/Fate Unveiling Imbued Items to pierce the Mask of a Briarwolf that somehow went to Ironside. Mystagogue leaders instead gain access to an Order Sanctum for casting more spells on their underlings (typically Unveiling, Shielding, Veiling and Perfecting) in preparation for track and capture missions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/924216-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-mountains-of-shadow?p=925424#post925424\" target=\"_blank\">Simurgh</a>, Mysterium Thyrsus in Mountains of Shadow (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/939031-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-mountains-of-shadow\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a>|<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/924216-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-mountains-of-shadow\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>)","edited":{"userid":6508,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6508-tambov","user":"Tambov","date":".  formatting 10-27-2025, 10:05 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6508-tambov","name":"Tambov","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6508_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"455"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-27T21:12:21-07:00","id":1554711,"title":"","content":"That's good, but I think it leans too much on Mage and Mage-specific rules. Even for STs with a good grasp of MtAw this can be a problem when the game isn't focused on them. I think there are many better generalist options for Merits that would fit, regardless of their ties to the Mysterium (which could itself be a mystery, not a direct statement).<br /> <br /> I would also change the specialty from Occult to Survival. Those are not detectives, they're hunters, they won't use much Occult to stalk their prey even if they do in preparation (and they only need one member in the group to be good at Occult, while several good survivalists is always good for hunters).<br /> <br /> For other Merits you can take Area of Expertise, Encyclopedic Knowledge (Cryptids), Interdisciplinary Specialty, Vice-Ridden (curiosity), Virtuous (curiosity), Greyhound, Seizing the Edge, Safe Place, Staff. Unseen Sense (for the most common type of creature in the area). Each of those says something about the group and the kind of person that comes to them. It's also imnportant to remember that Mystery Cult members, either as PCs or NPCs, will frequently work with other members of their cult, so any benefit should be something the group expects everyone in the hunting party to have, not just one or two specialists (this changes a little at higher levels, but not too much).<br /> <br /> Some Merits like Allies and Unseen Sense may work better if they're variable, changing according to the prey the group is focused on at the moment, indicating the group as a whole keeps many ties and many forms of training.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-06T10:26:39-08:00","id":1556246,"title":"","content":"It doesn't have to involve mages.<br /> <br /> It could just as easily be a demon's unwitting pawns gathering information on cryptids to better fight the God-Machine!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28921-creatorfoundermaker","name":"CreatorFounderMaker","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"91"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}